First, it isn’t true that the whole county’s water turned brown. The affected homes are likely a handful of properties near the construction site running on private wells, drawing straight from the ground with no utility or treatment plant in between.

The most-documented case is Beverly and Jeff Morris, whose house sits about 1,000 feet from Meta’s Stanton Springs campus on the Newton–Morgan county line.

@MatthewBerman: "AOC held up a jar of brown water in Congress and blamed a Meta data center. We happen to have a PhD in Environmental Health on the team, so he put her claims to the test. Here's his essay." The linked article provides a balanced look at AI’s environmental impact, data center costs, community burdens, and why responsible AI development matters.

